## 4. Dependency-file bandwidth management

### `set_bandwidth(local_file, ttype, bval)`
Only applies to `udp`/`vi`/`vo` (not `tcp`). Identify the target line inside
`dynamic_client.sh` by marker: `udp` → line containing `-u -b`; `vi` →
line containing `-S 0xA0`; `vo` → line containing `-S 0xE0`. On the
matching line(s), regex-replace `-b\s+\S+` with `-b {bval}`. Rewrite the
file if changed. Return whether a change was made.

### `_scp_dynamic_client(targets)`
scp `dynamic_client.sh` to each target's `ip:path/`, printing per-target
OK/FAILED.

### `configure_bandwidth_and_push(ttype)`
Interactive: for udp/vi/vo only, ask for a `-b` value (auto-append `M` unit
if the user typed a bare number), `ensure_local` the file, call
`set_bandwidth`, then ask "push to (1) all hardcoded devices or (2)
manually entered devices", and scp accordingly. This is a manual/legacy
path; the automated per-test-run bandwidth push is `auto_bandwidth_push`
(Section 6) which computes `-b` automatically instead of asking.

### `compute_bw(n)`
`f"{1200 // max(1, n)}M"` — divides a fixed 1200 Mbit budget evenly across
`n` clients.

### `auto_bandwidth_push(ttype, clients, script_name, targets)`
For udp/vi/vo: compute `bval = compute_bw(len(clients))`,
`ensure_local(script_name)`, `set_bandwidth`, then scp the updated script
to **all hardcoded lab devices** (`all_hardcoded_targets()`), not just the
clients in this run — so any device that later joins a test already has
the right file.

### `all_hardcoded_targets()`
Returns the full merged list of `{ip, path}` dicts built from `ALL_ASTRA`
+ `ALL_VIM3` (ASTRA_PATH / VIM3_PATH respectively). No `xx`/`type` keys
needed here — this is only used for blind scp pushes.

### `_scp_file(fname, targets)` / `ensure_local(fname)`
Generic scp-to-many and "write from TEMPLATES if missing" helpers used
throughout.

