## 9. Menu Option 8 — Memuse stress check (single run, deauth + rejoin)

`opt_memuse_stress()`. This test stresses SoftAP firmware memory handling
by deauthing a random subset of associated clients and watching them
auto-rejoin, capturing `wl memuse` at 3 points.

Shared helpers (also reused by Option 9):
- `_memuse_client_ips()` — all hardcoded clients (`ALL_ASTRA+ALL_VIM3`)
  EXCLUDING the DUT octet, as `{xx, ip, path}` dicts.
- `_collect_memuse(dut_ip, dut_path, logfile, tag)` — print a `--- {tag}
  (SoftAP {dut_ip}) ---` line, run `wl -i wlan1 memuse` on the DUT
  (output NOT suppressed — must print live during the run, no `, dp`
  suffix), append a tagged, timestamped, dashed block to `logfile`,
  return the raw stripped output text (callers keep `m1`/`m2`/`m3` for
  later use).
- `_get_ap_bssid(dut_ip, dut_path)` — `wl -i wlan1 status | grep BSSID` on
  the DUT (`, dp` suppressed — don't spam console with this), regex
  `BSSID:\s*([0-9a-fA-F:]{17})`.
- `_is_associated(host, path)` — `wl -i wlan0 status` on a client (`, dp`),
  True iff `"BSSID"` appears in the output.
- `_wpa_status(host, path)` — **NOTE**: despite the historical name (kept
  from an early iteration that checked `wpa_cli status` for the literal
  string `"address"`), this function was corrected mid-development to run
  `wl -i wlan0 status` and check for `"BSSID"` in the output — NOT
  `wpa_cli`. Any log text or print statement referencing this must say
  `wl -i wlan0 status` / `BSSID`, not `wpa_cli`/`address` (that was the old,
  wrong wording that got explicitly corrected).

Full flow:
1. Fresh `memuse.log` (`open(logfile, "w").close()` truncates), write a
   `#`-bordered header with DUT identity + timestamp.
2. **Discover associated clients**: for every hardcoded client, run
   `_is_associated`; collect the True ones into `assoc`, printing each as
   found. Abort with a message if `assoc` is empty. Log the associated-IP
   list.
3. **Pre-check ping** (added later as an explicit requirement): from the
   DUT, `ping -c 2 {data_ip}` for EVERY associated client (NOT suppressed
   — print raw ping output live), classify PING FAIL vs ping ok by
   checking for `"0 received"` / `" 0 packets received"` / empty output.
   This is informational only in the single-run version — it does NOT
   gate anything, purely printed for visibility before memuse #1.
4. **MEMUSE #1** — before deauth.
5. **Fetch AP_BSSID.** Abort if it can't be resolved.
6. **Ask the user how many STAs to deauth** (`k`, validated `1..len(assoc)`).
7. `picked = random.sample(assoc, k)` — **genuinely random subset each
   run**, not sequential/first-N. Log the BSSID and the picked IP list.
8. **Deauth**: for each picked client, `wl -i wlan0 deauthenticate
   {ap_bssid}` (`, dp` suppressed for the command noise, but print
   `"deauthed: {ip}"` per device).
9. **MEMUSE #2** — after deauth.
10. **Rejoin wait — NO timeout in this single-run version**: loop
    `while pending:`, poll `_wpa_status` on each pending client, move
    confirmed-rejoined ones out, sleep 3s between rounds, until the
    `pending` list is empty (i.e., this version blocks forever if a
    client never rejoins — intentional design choice for the single-run
    manual test, contrasted with the N-iteration version which DOES cap
    this at 15s per Section 10). Save each rejoined client's final `wl
    status` output in a `wpa_out` dict keyed by IP (name kept for
    historical reasons — holds `wl -i wlan0 status` output, not
    wpa_cli). Log the rejoined-IP list and per-STA raw status dump.
11. **Post-rejoin parallel ping via terminals** — build a `dut` dict
    (`{ip, path, data: SOFTAP_DATA}` — must use the `SOFTAP_DATA` constant,
    NOT a hardcoded `192.168.1.2`, which was an early bug that got fixed),
    assign `c["data"]` on every rejoined client, `start_ping(dut, rejoined,
    "d2c", "ping_rejoin")` (opens one terminal per client, genuinely
    parallel — this was an explicit requirement: real terminals, not
    background subprocess pings, so it visually matches the rest of the
    suite's terminal-based traffic style), sleep 13, `fetch_ping`. Parse
    each fetched file for `rtt min/avg/max/mdev` avg and the packet-summary
    line (`\d+ packets transmitted,.*`); if no rtt match, latency =
    `"NO DATA"`. Log a `--- DUT -> ip (data) avg=lat ms ---` block with the
    full raw output per client.
12. Sleep exactly 5s (settle time), then **MEMUSE #3** — after rejoin.
13. **One retry** for any client whose post-rejoin ping was `"NO DATA"`:
    rebuild the `failed` list, `start_ping`/sleep 13/`fetch_ping` again
    under a `"ping_retry"` prefix, parse the same way, tag each as PASS
    (has a real rtt) or FAIL, log a `--- RETRY ip (data) RESULT avg=lat
    ---` block per retried client. If nothing failed, just print/log "no
    retry needed" and skip.
14. **FLOW SUMMARY** appended to `memuse.log`: associated count, BSSID,
    deauthed count+IPs, rejoined count+IPs, the 3 memuse-capture tag
    labels, and a one-line retry outcome (`"N failed, P passed on retry"`
    or `"none needed"`).
15. Call `_memuse_excel(...)` to append the Excel block (see next).

