## 12. Menu assembly (`main()`)

A single dict `actions` mapping menu-number strings to `(label,
function)` tuples, iterated in insertion order to print the menu, `"0"`
exits. Final numbering (after all insertions/renumbering across the whole
build):
```
1  - Load driver on all DUTs        (Code A)
2  - Broadcast a command + collect  (Code B)
3  - Ping test (DUT <-> clients)
4  - TX traffic test  (DUT SoftAP -> clients)
5  - RX traffic test  (clients -> DUT SoftAP)
6  - Bidirectional traffic (DUT <-> clients)
7  - Combo: Ping + TX + RX + BD (one iteration)
8  - Memuse stress check (deauth + rejoin)
9  - Memuse stress check for N iterations (deauth + rejoin)
10 - Edit a dependency file + scp to devices
11 - Close all spawned terminals (keep this one)
12 - Push a custom file to all/selected devices
13 - Auto assign IPs to hardcoded devices
```
The main loop wraps each selected action's execution in a try/except:
`KeyboardInterrupt` → print "Interrupted -> back to menu." and continue
the loop (never exit the whole program on Ctrl-C during a sub-test);
any other `Exception` → print `f"ERROR: {e}"` and continue the loop (a
single test's crash must never kill the whole menu session).

