## 13. Non-negotiable behavioral rules recap (things that were explicitly corrected during development — do not reintroduce these bugs)

- `load.sh && supp.sh` must be `;` not `&&` (a non-zero load.sh exit must
  never block supp.sh from running).
- Driver-OK check triggers ONLY on `"adapter not found"` or `"command not
  found"` in `wl ver` output — never the generic word "error".
- Zero-throughput detection must parse the numeric mbps value and compare
  to `0.0`, never substring-match `"0.00"` against raw text (false
  positives inside e.g. `"10.00"`).
- SoftAP DUT is ALWAYS `172.16.1.4` / `192.168.1.4` / `/build` — never
  prompted for, never varied, and this exact data IP (not `.1.2` or any
  other placeholder) must be used everywhere a DUT data-plane IP is
  needed, including inside the memuse test's ping-setup dict.
- Rejoin/association detection is ALWAYS `wl -i wlan0 status` checked for
  the literal substring `"BSSID"` — never `wpa_cli status` / `"address"`
  (an earlier design used wpa_cli and was explicitly replaced).
- ARP verification must reject `<incomplete>` entries even if the IP
  substring is technically present — only a line with a real MAC pattern
  counts as resolved.
- In the N-iteration test, only a 7-second SSH TIMEOUT to a client
  constitutes "Device Crash" (permanent exclusion). Everything else
  (not associated, ping fail, rejoin-not-detected) is temporary and the
  client returns to the pool next iteration.
- The available-pool abort floor is `< k`, tied to the user's chosen
  deauth count — not any fixed number like 3.
- Excel for the N-iteration test must stay compact (Malloc+Free lines
  only, no full raw memuse dump) — the single-run test's Excel MAY dump
  full raw memuse line-by-line, but the N-iteration one must not, for
  workbook-size/performance reasons at ~1500 iterations.
- Output folders for the N-iteration test must auto-increment a `RunN`
  suffix, checked for existence before creating, and never silently
  overwrite a previous run's folder.
- The rebuild tool's ping-fail parser must NOT apply the retry-rescue
  logic, and its regex must handle the two-word `"NO DATA"` token
  correctly (`avg=(.+?) ms ---`, not `avg=(\S+) ms ---`).
- Terminal cleanup (`opt_close_terminals()`) in the N-iteration loop fires
  twice per iteration unconditionally: once right after the 5s settle
  before MEMUSE #3, and once right after the retry section whether or not
  a retry actually happened.

